I have a complete picture. Here is the detailed report.

---

# Codebase Report: `/home/cis/windows/realstate`

Next.js **16.3.0** App Router, React **19.2.8**, Tailwind v4. Relevant deps already installed: `three@0.185`, `@react-three/fiber@9.7`, `@react-three/drei@10.7`, `gsap@3.15` + `@gsap/react`, `lenis@1.3.26`, `framer-motion@13`, `pannellum`, `maplibre-gl`, `zod@4`, `react-hook-form`, `resend`. **No 3D asset loaders, no state library, no voice/speech deps.**

---

## 1. `app/layout.tsx` — provider nesting & where a gate mounts

104 lines. Fonts: `Fraunces` (400 only), `Manrope`, `Noto_Sans_Gujarati` (`preload:false`). Exports a static `metadata` object with `metadataBase`, title template `%s · ${siteConfig.name}`.

The exact tree (lines 73–104):

```tsx
export default function RootLayout({ children }: LayoutProps<"/">) {
  return (
    <html lang="en-IN" className={`${fraunces.variable} ${manrope.variable} ${notoGujarati.variable} h-full`}>
      <body className="flex min-h-full flex-col">
        <JsonLd data={organizationSchema()} />
        <ReducedMotionProvider>
          <MotionProvider>
            <LenisProvider />
            <a href="#main" className="… focus:z-[60] …">Skip to content</a>
            <SiteHeader />
            <FestiveBanner />
            {/* pb-16 clears the sticky mobile action bar. */}
            <main id="main" className="flex-1 pb-16 lg:pb-0">
              {children}
            </main>
            <SiteFooter />
            <WhatsAppFab />
            <StickyMobileActionBar />
          </MotionProvider>
        </ReducedMotionProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

Notes for slotting in an onboarding gate:

- **`LayoutProps<"/">`** and **`PageProps<"/projects/[slug]">`** are Next 16 *globally-injected* types — not imported. Follow that convention.
- Nesting order is `ReducedMotionProvider` → `MotionProvider` (framer `LazyMotion strict`) → everything. `LenisProvider` is a **sibling that renders `null`**, not a wrapper — it just runs an effect.
- **z-index ladder in use:** `SiteHeader` = `z-50` (`fixed inset-x-0 top-0`), `StickyMobileActionBar` = `z-50` (`fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 lg:hidden`), skip-link focus = `z-[60]`. `WhatsAppFab` is also fixed. A full-screen gate must sit **above `z-[60]`** (e.g. `z-[100]`) or it will be pierced by the header.
- The natural mount point for a gate is **immediately inside `<MotionProvider>`, before `<SiteHeader />`** — that way it is inside both the reduced-motion context and the framer feature boundary. If the gate needs to *suppress* Lenis, note `LenisProvider` reads only `useReducedMotionPreference()`; you'd need to extend it or lock `document.body.style.overflow` (the pattern `SiteHeader` already uses at lines 35–40 for its mobile sheet).
- `<body>` is `flex min-h-full flex-col`; a fixed-position overlay is unaffected, but a non-fixed gate would become a flex child.
- **`useSelectedLayoutSegment()` in `SiteHeader`**: `segment === null` means home route, which triggers the transparent-over-dark-hero treatment. A gate on `/` interacts with this.

