## 5. The four project components

**`unit-matrix.tsx`** (128 lines, **server component** — no `"use client"`). Props `{ towers: Tower[] }`. Per tower computes `perFloor = tower.units.length / tower.floors` and shows only `typicalFloor = units.slice(0, perFloor)` in a `<table>` (Unit letter via `String.fromCharCode(65+index)`, Type, Carpet area, Facing, From). Then `<FloorStack>` — a single CSS grid, `gridTemplateColumns: \`2rem repeat(${perFloor}, auto)\``, top floor first, one `<span className="unit-cell" data-status={unit.status} />` per unit (styled via `data-status` attribute in globals.css rather than per-cell classes, explicitly to cut HTML payload on 22-floor towers). Legend for available / blocked / sold. Its docblock says: *"Phase 3 replaces the tower headings with a clickable 3D master plan; this table stays underneath it as the fallback and as the crawlable version."*

**`progress-timeline.tsx`** (89 lines, server). Props `{ entries: Project["progress"] }`, returns `null` if empty. `<ol className="divide-y">`, each `<li>` a `grid sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr_120px]`: `formatMonth(entry.date)` | caption + stage label | `<StageGlyph>`. Two maps drive it — `STAGE_LABELS` (excavation→"Site works", foundation, structure→"Superstructure", finishing, handover) and **`STAGE_FILL` (excavation 0.1, foundation 0.3, structure 0.6, finishing 0.85, handover 1)**. `StageGlyph` draws a 6-floor SVG stack (`viewBox="0 0 40 48"`), filling `Math.round(6 * fill)` floors in `--forest`. **This `STAGE_FILL` ramp is the natural driver for a scroll-driven construction sequence** — it is already the site's canonical "how far up the building has got" scale.

**`cost-sheet.tsx`** (73 lines, server). Props `{ project, basePrice, carpetArea }`; calls `buildCostSheet({...})` from `lib/cost-sheet.ts` and renders `sheet.lines` (label + note + amount, `—` for zero) plus `sheet.total`, then a long statutory footnote branching on `sheet.gstExempt`. Explicitly server-rendered "so the numbers cannot be quietly recomputed on the client."

**`rera-block.tsx`** (71 lines, server). Props `{ project }`. Renders `siteConfig.rera.authority` + `project.reraNumber`, a link to `authorityUrl`, and a **dashed empty QR placeholder** (deliberately empty until a real registration exists). `isDemo = project.reraNumber === "DEMO-PENDING"` gates an extra §59 warning — **note the mismatch: the placeholder data actually uses `"AWAITING CLIENT"`, so `isDemo` is `false` for every project today.** Always renders the artist's-impression disclaimer.

