## 8. Storage usage — essentially none

Full-repo grep for `localStorage|sessionStorage|document.cookie|cookies()|indexedDB` returns **exactly three hits, all in one file**:

- `app/error.tsx:44` `if (sessionStorage.getItem(RELOAD_FLAG)) {`
- `app/error.tsx:49` `sessionStorage.setItem(RELOAD_FLAG, "1");`
- `app/error.tsx:56` `return () => sessionStorage.removeItem(RELOAD_FLAG);`

That is a one-shot reload guard in the error boundary. **There is no cookie usage, no `cookies()` from `next/headers`, no persistence layer, no consent/analytics storage anywhere.** So for remembering a name after the onboarding gate you are starting from zero — no existing helper, no key namespace, no hydration-safe storage hook. Two consequences worth planning for: (a) any storage read must be hydration-safe (the codebase's established answer is `useSyncExternalStore` with a server snapshot, as in `reduced-motion-provider.tsx`); (b) DPDP Act 2023 §6 consent framing is already taken seriously in `lib/enquiry-schema.ts` — storing a name will want the same treatment.

