## 9. Client state, context, personalization

**Context providers: exactly one.** `components/providers/reduced-motion-provider.tsx` — `createContext(false)`, read via `useSyncExternalStore` so the value is correct on first client render (server snapshot returns `false`). Exposed as `useReducedMotionPreference()`. Quoted intent: *"Every motion decision in the app reads this: Lenis stays off, GSAP degrades to fades, and the WebGL hero swaps for a static image."*

`MotionProvider` is a framer `<LazyMotion features={loadDomAnimation} strict>` boundary — **`strict` means importing `motion` instead of `m` throws.** Any new animated component must use `m.*`.

**No `zustand`, `jotai`, `redux`, or `useReducer` anywhere.** No `useContext` outside the reduced-motion module. **No user personalization, no auth, no session, no analytics.**

All client state is local `useState` in leaf components:
- `site-header.tsx` — `scrolled`, `menuOpen`; body-overflow lock; `useSelectedLayoutSegment()`.
- `project-filters.tsx` — the **only** URL-synced state: `usePathname` / `useRouter` / `useSearchParams`.
- `gallery-grid.tsx` — `category`, `project`, `lightboxIndex`.
- `testimonial-carousel.tsx` — `selected` (Embla).
- `floor-plan-viewer.tsx`, `master-plan-3d.tsx`, `emi-calculator.tsx`, `brochure-download.tsx`, `enquiry-form.tsx` — local.

**28 `"use client"` files total** out of ~60 components; everything else is a server component.

